WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.149
Not all telemetry is equally useful.

00:00:02.149 --> 00:00:06.795
Effective programs evaluate completeness, accuracy, timeliness, consistency, retention,

00:00:06.795 --> 00:00:08.796
normalization, enrichment, and coverage.

00:00:08.796 --> 00:00:12.740
A source can be connected and still fail to provide the fields or history analysts need

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.300
for a meaningful security question.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:18.090
Completeness asks whether expected systems and event types are represented.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:20.750
Accuracy considers whether fields, timestamps, identities,

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:22.600
and asset references are trustworthy.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.400
Timeliness measures whether events arrive quickly enough for detection and response,

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.495
while retention determines how far back an investigation can look.

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:33.130
Normalization helps teams compare different sources through consistent fields and

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:33.720
concepts.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:38.720
Enrichment adds business, asset, identity, vulnerability, threat, or geographic context.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.120
Both can improve analysis,

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.890
but teams should preserve enough original data to understand how a normalized event was

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:44.690
produced.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:48.600
Coverage analysis connects collection to threats, use cases, and critical services.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.500
Teams document blind spots, monitor source health, test expected events,

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.305
and review changes in architecture.

00:00:54.305 --> 00:00:58.800
Quality is an ongoing operational responsibility rather than a one-time onboarding task.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.700
Source-health measures make quality visible.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:04.800
Useful measures include expected-versus-reporting assets, event arrival delay,

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.655
parsing failures, missing fields, sudden volume changes, retention status,

00:01:08.655 --> 00:01:10.700
and the age of unresolved collection issues.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:14.810
Owners can use thresholds and review routines to detect degradation before an analyst

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:17.100
discovers it during a high-pressure investigation.
